WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.930
A vaccine can contain the very
germ that causes a disease,

2
00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:06.030
killed or made inactive.

3
00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:08.450
You might expect it to make you ill.

4
00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:11.590
Instead, it protects
you from that disease.

5
00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:15.870
So how can a dead or
inactive germ keep you safe?

6
00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:19.130
In this mission, you'll find
out how white blood cells make

7
00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:22.170
antibodies that fit the
antigens on a pathogen.

8
00:00:22.220 --> 00:00:24.390
You'll see what goes into a vaccine.

9
00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:28.870
And you'll discover why, if the
real pathogen arrives later,

10
00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:32.130
your immune system can respond
fast enough to stop you falling

11
00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:33.190
ill.

12
00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:37.050
Your mission: explain how
a vaccine protects you.
